From 9cbe53ce0034e9fd178ff62e4c4a95138f135345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil <300208363+calicopizzadelivery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:42:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] android: build the protocol library with Soong and host
 it over JNI

UxPlay's lib/ -- pairing, FairPlay (playfair), decryption, NTP timing,
llhttp -- built as libuxplay_airplay, and a JNI bridge, libuxplay_jni,
that takes the place of uxplay.cpp and the GStreamer renderers. The
receiving app (AirPlayReceiver in calicopizzadelivery/jetson-nano-android-tv)
decodes with MediaCodec and plays with AudioTrack; this side only hands
it finished frames.

- android/uxplay_jni.c: raop_callbacks_t turned into Java calls on
  org.lineageos.tv.airplay.UxPlay. Presentation times cross JNI already
  shifted from lib/'s CLOCK_REALTIME to CLOCK_MONOTONIC, the base of
  System.nanoTime() and MediaCodec's timed release. Threads UxPlay starts
  are attached lazily and detached by a pthread key destructor.
- android/dns_sd_android.c, android/include/dns_sd.h: the slice of the
  dns_sd API that lib/dnssd.c uses. UxPlay still builds its own TXT
  records; registering them is handed to the app, which uses NsdManager.
- android/alac: Android ships no ALAC decoder, so audio-only streams are
  decoded here, with David Hammerton's decoder (MIT) as carried by
  shairport-sync. AAC-ELD and AAC-LC go up encoded; Android decodes those.
- lib/crypto.c: pk_to_base64 with EVP_EncodeBlock. BoringSSL, the system
  libcrypto, declares BIO_f_base64 but does not implement it, so the BIO
  chain did not link. Same output, and no longer leaks the BUF_MEM.

libcrypto is linked dynamically: BoringSSL is used as the system crypto
library, which is what keeps GPLv3 and its licence compatible here.
libplist comes from calicopizzadelivery/libplist, which adds its build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
